1. A client says: "Web Content should not be published directly. Department Head must approve it first." How will you implement this?
I will enable workflow for Web Content from Workflow Configuration. I will create/update a Kaleo workflow definition where:
User submits Web Content
Content goes into Pending state
Review task is assigned to Department Head role
Department Head approves/rejects
On approval, content moves to Approved state and becomes visible
Draft → Pending → Review → Approved / Rejected


2. What happens internally when workflow is enabled and user creates Web Content?
-)Liferay creates the content entry.
-)Initial status becomes WorkflowConstants.STATUS_PENDING.
-)Kaleo creates a workflow instance.
-)Workflow task is generated.
-)Task is assigned based on workflow configuration.
-)Reviewer completes the task.
On approval:
Status changes to APPROVED
Content becomes available

